hyp spec: the one spec of hyp. hyp acts on each entry below, so a change to a
rule is a change to its entry.

events: each kind, where it is stored, the Goal it belongs to, whether an end
freezes it, and the act that writes it
  goal.add  stored in git  Goal: the Goal it adds, or the written Goal it replaces  frozen by an end: yes  written by: add goal
  example.place  stored in git  Goal: the Goal its node names; the old form of a place, replayed and no longer written  frozen by an end: yes  written by: none
  examples.place  stored in git  Goal: the Goal its node names  frozen by an end: yes  written by: place
  result.record  stored in git  Goal: the Goal its node names  frozen by an end: yes  written by: run
  result.retract  stored in git  Goal: the Goal of the Result its node names  frozen by an end: yes  written by: retract, not built
  select  stored in git  Goal: the Goal its node names  frozen by an end: yes  written by: select
  budget.reset  stored in git  Goal: the Goal its node names  frozen by an end: no  written by: reset, not built
  land  stored in git  Goal: the Goal its node names; it ends the Goal  frozen by an end: no  written by: land
  close  stored in git  Goal: the Goal its node names; it ends the Goal  frozen by an end: no  written by: close
  unselect  stored in git  Goal: the Goal its node names  frozen by an end: yes  written by: unselect
  read  stored in trace  Goal: none: it is what hyp printed to an actor, and changes no Goal  frozen by an end: no  written by: every command that names an actor

states: each state, when it holds, the acts hyp status may offer in it, and
each act it does not allow with the guard that stops that act
  written  holds when: a goal.add exists, and the Goal is not open
  written  allows: add goal, place, run, close
  written  does not allow: run, on a commit that is not H0 (guard Open); select, no row is met yet (guard Candidate); land, a written Goal has no stop (guard Stop); unselect, the Goal has no select (guard Selected)
  open  holds when: every line holds a placed example, and every current example gives on H0 the verdict its line's kind needs
  open  allows: place, run, select, land, close
  open  does not allow: add goal, a replace (guard Draft); select, a row that is not a candidate (guard Candidate); select, the runner's, after an unselect with no new cell since (guard New cell); land, while the Goal has no stop (guard Stop); unselect, the Goal has no select (guard Selected)
  selected  holds when: the Goal has a select that no unselect undid, and no end
  selected  allows: land, unselect, close
  selected  does not allow: add goal, a replace (guard Draft); add goal, --from G (guard From ended); place (guard Selected); run (guard Selected); select (guard Selected)
  ended  holds when: the Goal has a land or a close
  ended  allows: none
  ended  does not allow: add goal, a replace (guard Draft); place (guard Not ended); run (guard Not ended); select (guard Not ended); land (guard Not ended); unselect (guard Not ended); close (guard Not ended)

acts: each command, its usage, its roles, the states that allow it, its
guards in order, and what it writes
  add goal  usage: add goal [G] --base COMMIT --words TEXT --line gap:TEXT [--line guard:TEXT ...]  roles: owner  states: written  guards in order: Draft, Whole lines, From ended  writes: goal.add; a new Goal is in no state before it
  place  usage: place G [--why TEXT]  roles: grill  states: written, open  guards in order: Not ended, Selected, Grill places, Whole set, Committed, Adds only, Kind  writes: examples.place
  run  usage: run COMMIT G/LINE [--why TEXT]  roles: runner  states: written, open  guards in order: Not ended, Selected, Bytes, Open, Own path, Leaf only, Budget, Stable  writes: result.record
  try  usage: try G LINE/EXAMPLE [--worktree]  roles: any, a read  guards: none  writes: a read event in the trace
  select  usage: select G HASH [--why TEXT]  roles: runner, owner  states: open  guards in order: Not ended, Selected, Candidate, New cell, Goal's actor, Spec, Own path  writes: select
  land  usage: land G [--why TEXT]  roles: owner  states: open, selected  guards in order: Not ended, Owner lands, Goal's actor, Stop  writes: land
  close  usage: close G [--why TEXT]  roles: owner  states: written, open, selected  guards in order: Not ended, Owner closes, Goal's actor  writes: close
  unselect  usage: unselect G [--why TEXT]  roles: owner  states: selected  guards in order: Not ended, Owner unselects, Goal's actor, Selected  writes: unselect
  status  usage: status [G] [--role ROLE]  roles: any, a read  guards: none  writes: a read event in the trace
  show  usage: show ACTOR  roles: any, a read  guards: none  writes: a read event in the trace
  prune  usage: prune [--remove]  roles: any, a read  guards: none  writes: a read event in the trace
  spec  usage: spec  roles: any, a read with no actor  guards: none  writes: nothing
  help  usage: help  roles: any, a read with no actor  guards: none  writes: nothing
  version  usage: version  roles: any, a read with no actor  guards: none  writes: nothing

guards: each guard, its rule, and the codes of the refusals it gives, each
with exit 1
  Draft  rule: before the Goal opens, add goal G may replace it; after, its words and lines are frozen; a new Goal always passes  codes: no-goal-to-replace, not-written  exit 1
  Whole lines  rule: every line has a kind, gap or guard; the Goal has one to ten lines and at least one gap line  codes: too-many-lines, bad-line-kind, no-gap-line, payload-invalid  exit 1
  From ended  rule: add goal --from G cites only an ended Goal, landed or closed; checked by the act only, never at replay  codes: from-not-ended  exit 1
  Not ended  rule: no write after the owner's land or close ends the Goal; replay also stops an event of the Goal ahead of the end that the end's snapshot does not name  codes: ended, not-in-snapshot  exit 1
  Selected  rule: place, run and select need the Goal to have no select; unselect needs it to have one  codes: has-select, no-select, payload-invalid  exit 1
  Grill places  rule: only the grill places an example  codes: not-grill, payload-invalid  exit 1
  Whole set  rule: the set of a place is every folder goals/G/LINE/EXAMPLE; every line holds an example folder, every placed example keeps its folder, and every folder's name is an example name  codes: line-holds-no-example, placed-folder-gone, not-an-example-name  exit 1
  Committed  rule: each example folder's bytes on disk equal its bytes committed at HEAD  codes: not-a-folder, folder-on-disk, not-committed, disk-not-committed, differs-at, set-changed-while-probe  exit 1
  Adds only  rule: a new version of an example only adds floor or ceiling sections; any other change is a new example key; a hash the key held before never comes back; a place that changes no example places nothing  codes: set-unchanged, key-twice-in-set, already-current, earlier-version, section-differs, path-differs, drops-floor, drops-ceiling, adds-nothing  exit 1
  Kind  rule: H0 gives each changed example the verdict its line's kind needs: a gap example fails, a guard example is met  codes: wrong-verdict-on-h0, h0-moved-while-placing  exit 1
  Bytes  rule: the commit exists in this clone  codes: commit-not-here, not-a-commit  exit 1
  Open  rule: the Goal is open, unless the commit's subject hash is H0's; the examples do not change while the Probes run  codes: nothing-placed, not-open, h0-moved-while-run, examples-changed, example-changed  exit 1
  Own path  rule: the runner's own change of the commit writes no path under goals/X/ of another Goal X  codes: other-goal-path  exit 1
  Leaf only  rule: a run is on H0, or on a commit that no row of the Goal descends from  codes: ancestor-of-row  exit 1
  Budget  rule: at most three Hypotheses run since the boundary, H0 never counted  codes: budget-used  exit 1
  Stable  rule: two runs on the same bytes give one verdict; a run it stops still records its Result, marked, which counts nothing  codes: other-verdict, verdicts-differed, payload-invalid  exit 1
  Candidate  rule: the row is a candidate, a leaf row met on every line; with two or more candidates only the owner selects  codes: role-cannot-select, no-row, owner-selects-among, row-not-leaf, row-not-met, row-not-met-on-goal, no-result-on-row  exit 1
  New cell  rule: after an unselect, the runner selects only once a run recorded a cell whose example version, or whose row, had not run before it; the owner selects at any time  codes: no-new-cell  exit 1
  Goal's actor  rule: only the actor that added the Goal selects for the owner, lands, closes or unselects it  codes: not-goals-actor  exit 1
  Spec  rule: the selected commit holds a spec under goals/G/specs/; a model there names each rule of its check configs in a variant config, and holds a chart  codes: no-spec, rule-no-variant, no-chart  exit 1
  Owner lands  rule: only the owner lands a Goal  codes: not-owner  exit 1
  Stop  rule: a land needs a stop: selected, two candidates or budget used  codes: no-stop, stop-not-held, payload-invalid  exit 1
  Owner closes  rule: only the owner closes a Goal, at any stop or none  codes: not-owner-close, payload-invalid  exit 1
  Owner unselects  rule: only the owner unselects a Goal  codes: not-owner-unselect, payload-invalid  exit 1
  Own Result  rule: only the actor that ran a Result retracts it  codes: not-own-result  exit 1
  (no guard)  rule: a file hyp reads breaks a rule of its form, or the act names what the store does not hold  codes: no-store, event-version, event-type, payload-decode, payload-invalid, trailing-data, id-not-ulid, actor-not-file, no-id-after, no-goal-to-place, no-goal-to-run, no-goal-to-select, no-goal-to-land, no-goal-to-close, no-goal-to-unselect, no-result-to-retract, no-example-txtar, text-before-first, second-section, external-not-name, input-outside, input-twice, unknown-section, no-section, submodule, entry-leaves, not-file-or-dir, read-folder  exit 1
  a place that places none of its set gives set-not-placed, with the guard of its first cause  exit 1

exit codes:
  exit 0  recorded or printed: the act recorded its event, or the read printed
  exit 1  refusal: a rule of hyp refuses the act, or a file hyp reads breaks a rule; the refusal names its guard
  exit 2  bad argument: the command line is wrong
  exit 3  environment problem: I/O, a missing tool, or a Probe that failed or timed out

rules:
  the store
    The store is .tree/ at the git top level: .tree/events/<actor>.jsonl, one file per actor, appended only, and .tree/outputs/<sha256>.
    The first add goal creates it; .tree/.gitattributes merges the events files by union.
    The trace is $HOME/.hyp/traces/<sha256 of the clone's git common directory>/: every command that names an actor records there what hyp printed to it, before it prints.
  merge order and replay
    Replay reads every event by id, then by actor, then by line bytes, and calculates every table and state on every command; no state is stored.
    Replay checks each event's guards again at its place; an event that fails them is listed under refused at replay and never deleted.
    An end names its snapshot, the Goal's events replay applied when the owner ended it; an event of a kind an end freezes that the snapshot does not name is stopped by Not ended.
  ids, actors and roles
    An event id is a ULID; a Goal id is G- and the last six characters of its goal.add id, a Result id R- and six.
    An actor matches ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,39}$ and names its events file; a write act needs a role: owner, grill, probe-writer or runner.
  the subject
    A commit's subject is its tree without the top-level entries goals and .tree; its git tree hash is the subject hash, one Hypothesis, one row.
    H0 is the Goal's base commit; a row is a leaf when none of its commits has a descendant among the commits of the Goal's other rows.
  budget and stops
    The budget is three Hypotheses since the boundary, H0 never counted; a refused run costs nothing, a retracted Result still counts.
    The boundary is the latest of the latest place, the latest budget.reset and the latest unselect, else the Goal's start.
    The stops: selected (a select), two candidates (two or more candidates and no select), budget used (three Hypotheses counted, the third with a live cell for every example, and no candidate).
    A stop is calculated, never stored; it waits for the owner. At two candidates and budget used the state block adds the table of outputs.
  the example file
    An example is goals/G/LINE/EXAMPLE/ with example.txtar and probe/. Its sections: words (one), input/<path> (any), run (one), floor: contains and floor: equals (one or more floors), ceiling (any), external (at most one).
    One literal per section, byte for byte; a section body's final newline does not count.
    An example is met when the output holds every floor and contains no ceiling, else failed; a line is met on a row when every placed example of it is met there.
  the Probe
    hyp runs probe/run with empty stdin and a 10 minute timeout, in a fresh copy of the commit's subject ($HYP_SUBJECT), with $HYP_EXAMPLE a copy of the example folder and $HYP_RUN the run section.
    Only PATH, HOME and the names of the external section pass from the environment.
    The Probe prints the stdout of run, then a last line exit N; the output is the rest, with one final newline dropped. Its stderr is kept beside it and never compared.
    A Probe that exits non-zero, times out or prints no exit line records nothing: exit 3.
every refusal names the guard hyp spec names
hyp status offers only acts hyp spec allows